# Entry point and daemon assembly

- `cmd/golem-deploy` parses subcommands with stdlib `flag` (`serve`, `admin create|reset-password`, `version`; no arguments prints usage and exits 2). Flags have `GOLEM_DEPLOY_*` environment fallbacks; there is no config file. Never prompt on stdin during `serve`.
- `internal/daemon.Run` is the composition root: data directory, keys, store, `Reconcile`, git runner (with startup sweeps of git scratch files and orphaned checkouts; nil when git is missing), `store.ReconcileBuilds`, static store (with `--static-quota-mb`), job runner (4 workers for server and project jobs plus the `build.JobPool` pool of `build.MaxActiveBuilds` workers, because waiting builds hold one), instance id (`store.InstanceID`), env-file and build-directory sweeps (`docker.SweepEnvFiles`, `build.SweepTemp`), `docker.Client` (also the `/status` probe, with a separate `layout.BuildDockerConfig()` for builds), the certificate manager (`certs.Open` on `layout.GameCerts()`, refused when the path cannot be bind-mounted; one `Check` before serving and `Maintain` hourly until shutdown, stopped before the store closes), the ephemeral-range warning (`ports.EphemeralOverlap`), `build.Service` (`--build-timeout` 1m–24h default 30m, `--build-retention` 1–100 default 5), `servers.Service` (default game host = first valid `--public-host`), `httpapi.Server`; after listening it runs `servers.Reconcile` in the background (start jobs for servers that should run, with `servers.WithJobID`). The build-image cleanup retry loop starts after build reconciliation and stops before the store closes. On context cancellation HTTP shutdown and job cancellation run together and the store closes last. Before touching disk it validates the network configuration: plaintext HTTP only on loopback (`httpapi.CheckListen`, which resolves `localhost`), `--public-host` (`httpapi.NormalizePublicHosts`) `--trusted-proxy` (`httpapi.ParseTrustedProxies`) and the server settings (`--port-range`, `--port-bind-address`, `--server-memory-mb` default 2048, `--server-cpus` default 2, `--static-quota-mb` default 5120; 0 means unlimited; `--start-timeout` default 60s, 1s–30m), `--max-repo-size-mb` and that the data directory path fits the git SSH configuration (`git.CheckSSHConfigPath`); comma-separated flag values are split by `splitList` in `main.go`. Right after `datadir.Prepare` it takes `datadir.AcquireLock` (held until exit), before reconciliation and the startup sweeps; the `admin` commands never take the lock.
- `internal/datadir` owns the data directory layout. The data directory is dedicated: `Prepare` accepts a missing or empty directory (lone `lost+found` allowed), one with the `.golem-deploy-data` marker (format line; written 0600 on initialisation) or a pre-marker data directory with only layout entries and the database; `Open` (admin reset-password) requires the marker and creates nothing, `admin create` uses `Prepare`. Missing directories are created 0700, existing ones are never chmodded (on Unix a group/world-accessible data directory is refused with the `chmod 700` to run), the database file is pre-created 0600, key files are 0600 and refused on Unix when readable by group or others. All runtime paths come from `datadir.Layout`; nothing is written relative to the working directory.
- `internal/daemon/admin.go` backs the `admin` CLI and works while the daemon runs (SQLite WAL). `reset-password` ends sessions and deletes the account's API tokens; its output must say exactly that.
- `frontend/embed.go` embeds `frontend/dist` (`all:dist`); without `index.html` it serves a plain-text 503 notice. Only paths outside `/api/` reach it.
- Changes to flags, environment variables or the data directory layout must update `README.md`.
- Verify with `go test ./cmd/... ./internal/daemon/... ./internal/datadir/... ./frontend/...`.
